---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Plain-language pilot terms for The Buying Desk by Teardown Cafe."
>
  <div class="desk-page desk-prose">
    <header class="desk-page-header">
      <p class="desk-eyebrow">Pilot terms / plain language</p>
      <h1>Clear scope before work.</h1>
      <p>
        These are the pilot rules in plain English. They havent had a legal
        polish. The email where we agree on scope, timing, and price is what
        counts for that request.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>A request is not an order</h2>
      <p>
        Sending a request starts a conversation. I'll first check whether I can
        answer it, what I'll deliver, how long it'll take, and the price.
        Nothing starts until we both agree by email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Advice, not a guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        I give you my best judgment using what's available at the time. Listings
        can be wrong. Prices move. A remote check cant guarantee condition,
        safety, authenticity, seller conduct, compatibility, or future
        reliability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your part</h2>
      <p>
        Provide accurate context and don’t knowingly send private information
        belonging to someone else. You remain responsible for the purchase,
        seller verification, payment method, inspection, safe use, and any final
        decision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Remote service boundary</h2>
      <p>
        Inspect It isnt available during this pilot. Unless we agree otherwise
        in writing, this is remote research. It isnt a physical inspection,
        repair, lab test, financial advice, or warranty.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:amasud.tech@gmail.com">amasud.tech@gmail.com</a>
        before agreeing if anything is unclear.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
